      "guideBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "This is the original VirusMike V2 archive, with its injector, Multiplayer and Zombies scripts, INI example and readme. Extract it before use. The source lists BO3 game update 01.33 and CUSA03004, CUSA02290 or CUSA02624. These are source-stated requirements, not a physical-console test."
        },
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Prepare the supplied files",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Extract and match your game",
              "text": "Keep the original RAR. Extract its folders and check your installed BO3 title ID and game update. Use the matching GoldHEN environment supported by your console firmware."
            },
            {
              "title": "Place the selected injector",
              "text": "Copy this pack's T7_GSC_Injector.prx to /data/GoldHEN/plugins/. Preserve an existing injector with the same filename before changing it; the previously archived standalone build is different."
            },
            {
              "title": "Merge only the matching plugin entry",
              "text": "In /data/GoldHEN/plugins.ini, add /data/GoldHEN/plugins/T7_GSC_Injector.prx only under your installed BO3 CUSA section. Preserve existing entries. The pack's INI also names BO3-Customs and DeadOps plugins that are not included here, and repeats some sections; do not copy that entire INI over your configuration."
            },
            {
              "title": "Place the menu scripts",
              "text": "Copy the supplied T7 GSC Injector folder and its scripts to /data/T7 GSC Injector/. That directory is present as a literal path in this pack's PRX. Keep the MP and ZM filenames so you can select the intended mode."
            },
            {
              "title": "Select and inject from the lobby",
              "text": "Enable your configured GoldHEN plugin loading, then launch the matching game. The included readme says to select and inject a menu while in the game lobby before starting the match. It permits adding or removing menu files while the game is open."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The readme makes a broad firmware claim, but no specific firmware matrix or native PS5 instructions are supplied. Use the requirements of your compatible GoldHEN release. Preserve the source readme and all older archived builds."
        }
      ],
